
🚀 Multiprocessing Backup Automation with rsync


📌 Overview

This project contains an automated data synchronization solution built for a media production studio. The system replaces a slow, single-threaded backup loop with a high-performance Python multiprocessing script that utilizes all available CPU cores to sync individual project folders concurrently via rsync.

The Problem

• The studio's storage grew rapidly, making daily backups from the Production NAS (~/data/prod) to the Backup NAS (~/data/prod_backup) take more than 20 hours.
• Initial performance profiling revealed that the script was bottlenecked by a single-core constraint (CPU-bound operational logic), leaving multiple server cores idle while executing file transfers sequentially.

